hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"6640","The narrator states) The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) joined his index finger and middle finger together as he said this."
"6641","“I and the Hour have been sent like these two,” and he held up his two fingers together. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4040)"
"6642","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said to Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him): ""Are you not pleased that your relation to me is like that of Sayyiduna Harun (peace be upon him) to Sayyiduna Musa (peace be upon him)? However, there will be no prophet after me."
"6643","The Prophet said to 'Ali: ""Would it not please you to be to me as Harun was to Musa?"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 115)"
"6644","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) has sent me with the declaration of disassociation (Bara’ah), which I will recite before the people at the time of Hajj. (The narrator says:) Then we reached Makkah. One day before Tarwiyah, Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) stood up and delivered a sermon to the people (explaining the rulings of Hajj). When he finished, Sayyiduna ‘Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) stood up. He recited Surah Tawbah and completed it in full. Then we set out with them, until when the day of ‘Arafah came, Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) stood up and delivered a sermon to the people, teaching them the rites of Hajj. When he finished, Sayyiduna ‘Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) stood up and recited Surah Tawbah before the people until he completed it. Then when the day of sacrifice came and we returned, when Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) returned, he delivered a sermon to the people, informing them about returning, about sacrifice, and about other rites. When he finished, Sayyiduna ‘Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) stood up and recited Surah Bara’ah before the people until he completed it. When the day of the first departure came, Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) stood up and delivered a sermon to the people. He informed the people how they should depart and how they should perform the stoning (rami). He taught the people the rites of Hajj. When he finished, Sayyiduna ‘Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) stood up and recited Surah Tawbah before the people until he completed its recitation."
"6645","when the Prophet came back from the Umrah of Al-Jirranah, he sent Abu Bakr to lead the Hajj. We wnet the him until, when he was in Al-Urj, the Iqamah for Subh was said, and he stood up to say the Takbir while he heard the grunting of a camel behind him, and he did not say the Takbir. He said: ""This is the grunting of the camel of the Messenger of Allah has had second thoughts about the Hajj, and may be he is here, and we will pray with him."" But it was 'Ali on the camel. Abu Bakr said to him: ""(Have you come) as a leader or as messenger?"" He said: ""No, as a messenger, sent by the Messenger of Allah with a declaration of innocence to recite it to the people in the stations of Hajj. So we came to makkah and one day before the day of At-Tarwiyah Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, stood up and addressed the people telling them about their rituals. When he finished, Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, stood up and recited the declaration of innocence to the people until he finished it. Then we went out with hm and on the day of Arafat. Abu Bakr stood up and addressed people, telling them about rituals. When he finished, Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, stood up and recited the declaration of innocence to the people until he finished it. Then on the day of Sacrifice, we departed (Ifadah) and when Abu Bakr came back, eh addressed the people, telling them about their departure (Ifadah), sacrifice and rituals. When he finished, Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, stood up and recited the declaration of innocence to the people until he finished it. On the first day of An-Nafr (The 12th of Dhul-Hijjah), Abu Bakr stood up and addressed the people, telling them how to offer their sacrifice and how to stone the Jamrat, and teaching them their rituals. When he had finished, ""Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, stood up and recited the declaration of innocence to the people until he finished it. (Daif) Abu Abdur-Rahman (An-Nasai) said: Ibn Khuthaim is not strong in Hadith, and I only narrated this so it would not be considered to be from Ibn Juraij from Abu Az-Zubai. And we did not write it except from Ishaq bin Rahuyah bin Ibrahm. And yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan did not abandon the narrations of Ibn Khuthaim, or dod Abdur-Rahamn. However, Ali bin Al-Madini said: ""Ibn Khuthaim is Munkar in Hadith,"" and Ali bin Al-Madini is more knowledgeable of Hadith. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2993)"
"6646","narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Indeed, when Allah the Exalted intends to show mercy to any nation among His servants, He takes the soul of their Prophet before them and makes that Prophet a forerunner and the first to go before them. And when He intends to destroy any nation, He afflicts them with punishment while their Prophet is still alive, so He cools the eyes of that Prophet through the destruction of those people, when they declare that Prophet to be a liar and disobey his command.”"
"6647","When Allah, the Exalted and Glorious, intends to show mercy to an Umma from amongst His servants He calls back His Apostle to his eternal home and makes him a harbinger and recompense in the world to come; and when He intends to cause destruction to an Umma, He punishes it while its Apostle is alive and He destroys it as he (the Apostle) witnesses it and he cools his eyes by destruction as they had belied him and disobeyed his command. (Using translation from Muslim 2288)"
"6648","I heard Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying while pointing his hands towards the east: The turmoil would appear from this side; verily, the turmoil would appear from this side (he repeated it thrice) where appear the horns of Satan. (Using translation from Muslim 2905e)"
"6649","Behold, turmoil would appear from this side, from where the horns of Satan would appear. (Using translation from Muslim 2905a)"
"6650","The Hour will not be established until thirty Dajjals appear, each of them claiming that he is the Messenger of Allah, until wealth becomes widespread, trials will become apparent, and killing will be abundant."" The people asked: ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! What is meant by 'harj'?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied: ""Killing, killing."
"6651","narrates: Before the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said anything about Musaylimah the Liar, people used to talk a lot about his matter. Then the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) stood among the people, praised Allah as is His due, and then said: ""To proceed! As for the matter of this person about whom you often talk, he is one of the thirty liars who will appear before the Dajjal, and the trial of the Dajjal will enter every city except Madinah Munawwarah. It will not enter it, because at every entrance of it there are two angels appointed who keep the Dajjal's influence away from it."
"6656","The Caliphate will last for thirty years, after that there will be kings. The caliphs and kings will be twelve."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) This is the narration that has caused confusion for the one who does not have expertise in the science of hadith, and he says that its last part contradicts its first part, because the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) stated that the caliphate will last for thirty years, then he said: after that, all will be kings. So, after thirty years, whoever becomes the caretaker of the affairs of the Muslims, all those people will be considered kings. Then the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: the number of caliphs and kings will be twelve. So the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) limited the number of caliphs and kings to only twelve. Therefore, apparently, it seems that these words are contrary to the initial part. However, by the grace and mercy of Allah Almighty, this is not the case, and it is not necessary that if a person is deprived of the ability to reach a correct proof, he should start declaring the transmitted narrations as incorrect. Rather, it is necessary that he should acquire knowledge from its original sources and gain understanding about the Sunnah, so that he may know that the one who is infallible and does not speak from his own desire, but only speaks what is revealed to him, there is no contradiction or difference in his statements. According to us, the meaning of this narration is that after thirty years, the rulers who will come can be called caliphs out of necessity (i.e., in a state of compulsion), even though in reality they will be kings, and the last of these twelve caliphs is Umar ibn Abdul Aziz. When the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) mentioned that the true caliphate will last for thirty years, and then after that, the last of the twelve caliphs is Umar ibn Abdul Aziz, then he will be counted among the rightly guided caliphs. So, those who came between him and the first four caliphs, the word caliphs has been used for them. The situation is as follows: when Allah Almighty took the blessed soul of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and transferred him to Paradise, this was on Monday night, the night of 12th Rabi' al-Awwal, 11 AH. After that, on the second day after the passing of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), that is, on Tuesday, Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) was chosen as caliph. Then Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) passed away on the night of 17th Jumada al-Thani. His caliphate lasted two years, three months, and twenty-two days. After that, the next day, that is, the day after the passing of Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), Sayyiduna Umar ibn Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) was chosen as caliph. Then Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) was martyred. His caliphate lasted ten years, six months, and four days. Then Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (may Allah be pleased with him) became caliph. Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) was martyred, so his caliphate lasted twelve years, less twelve days. Then Sayyiduna Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) was made caliph; he was martyred. His caliphate lasted five years and three months, less fourteen days. When Sayyiduna Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) was martyred, it was the 17th of Ramadan, 40 AH. After that, the people of Kufa pledged allegiance to Sayyiduna Imam Hasan (may Allah be pleased with him), and the people of Sham pledged allegiance to Sayyiduna Muawiyah ibn Abu Sufyan (may Allah be pleased with him) in Aaliya. Then Sayyiduna Muawiyah set out towards Kufa (for battle), and Sayyiduna Imam Hasan ibn Ali (may Allah be pleased with them both) set out towards him. Near Anbar, both met, and they made peace under an agreement with certain conditions. So Sayyiduna Imam Hasan (may Allah be pleased with him) handed over the matter of government to Sayyiduna Amir Muawiyah. This was on Monday, 25th Rabi' al-Awwal, 41 AH. This year was called the year of unity. Then Sayyiduna Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) passed away in Damascus; this was on Monday, 22nd Rajab al-Murajjab, 60 AH. His rule lasted 19 years and a little less than four months. When he passed away, he was 78 years old. After that, his son Yazid ibn Muawiyah became his successor on Monday, the same day his father passed away. He died in Hawarin, which is a village of Damascus; this was on 14th Rabi' al-Awwal, 64 AH. At that time, he was 38 years old, and his rule lasted three years, eight months, and a few days less. Then his son Muawiyah ibn Yazid was pledged allegiance to on 15th Rabi' al-Awwal, 64 AH. He died on 25th Rabi' al-Thani, 64 AH. His rule lasted 40 days. When he died, he was 21 years old. Then the people of Sham pledged allegiance to Marwan ibn Hakam, and the people of Hijaz pledged allegiance to Abdullah ibn Zubair. Then, on Wednesday, 3rd Dhu al-Qi'dah, 64 AH, Marwan became the complete ruler. Marwan ibn Hakam died in the month of Ramadan in Damascus in 65 AH. At that time, he was 63 years old, and his rule lasted a little less than ten months. Then the people of Sham pledged allegiance to Abdul Malik ibn Marwan, on the same day his father died. Abdul Malik died in Damascus in Shawwal, 86 AH. At that time, he was 62 years old. Then the people of Sham pledged allegiance to his son Walid, on the same day Abdul Malik died. Then Walid died in Damascus on 15th Jumada al-Thani, 96 AH. On the day he died, he was 48 years old, and his rule lasted nine years and eight months. Then allegiance was pledged to Sulayman ibn Abdul Malik, who was his real brother. Sulayman died at the place of Dabiq on Friday, 10th Safar, 99 AH. At that time, he was 45 years old, and his rule lasted two years, eight months, and five days. Then the people pledged allegiance to Umar ibn Abdul Aziz on the same day Sulayman died. Umar ibn Abdul Aziz died in the land of Homs at the place of ""Dayr Sim'an"" on Friday, 5th Rajab al-Murajjab, 101 AH. On the day he died, he was 41 years old, and his caliphate lasted two years, five months, and five days. He was the last of those twelve caliphs about whom the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) informed his Ummah."
"6657","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Soon after me there will be caliphs who will act according to what they know and will do what they have been commanded, and after them there will be other caliphs who will act without knowledge and will do things they were not commanded to do. Whoever rejects them will be free of blame, and whoever keeps himself away from them will remain safe, but the one who is pleased with them and follows them, his matter is different."
"6658","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) is also transmitted with another chain of narration.(Imam Ibn Hibba"
"6662","I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Islam will continue to be triumphant until there have been twelve Caliphs. Then the Prophet ﷺ said something which I could not understand. I asked my father: What did he say? He said: He has said that all of them (twelve Caliphs) will be from the Quraish. (Using translation from Muslim 1821d)"
"6663","The mill of Islam will keep turning for 35 years. (The narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words) 36 years. If those people are destroyed, then it will be according to the way in which they were destroyed, and if they remain, then their religion will remain for them for seventy years.” (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) This is the narration because of which the people of innovation criticize our Imams, and they say that the hadith scholars belong to the Hashwiyyah sect. They narrate such things which are incorrect in terms of reflection and perception, and the hadith scholars even declare them authentic. Then if they are asked about the description of this thing, they say: We believe in it but we do not explain it. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) By the grace and mercy of Allah, we are not like that, nor are we as we are accused of being. Rather, we say that in all the matters in which the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed his Ummah, there is nothing that cannot be understood, and in his Sunnahs there is no such Sunnah whose meaning cannot be known. Whoever thinks that when a Sunnah is authentically transmitted, it is necessary to narrate it and to have faith in it, even though it is not explained or its meaning is not understood, then such a person is criticizing the Messengerhood. O Allah (only Your help can be sought). However, among the hadiths there are some narrations in which the attributes of Allah Almighty are mentioned, whose reality cannot be described, but it is obligatory for people to have faith in those attributes. According to us, the meaning of this narration is as we have mentioned in our books, that sometimes the Arabs use the name of the whole thing for one of its parts. Similarly, in their idiom, the Arabs use the word ‘end’ for the ‘beginning’ and the word ‘beginning’ for the ‘end’. So the statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), “The mill of Islam will keep turning for 35 years (the narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words) 36 years,” by this he meant that the government would transfer from Banu Hashim to Banu Umayyah, because at the end of 36 Hijri, the government went to both of them. So when this matter became problematic for Banu Hashim and Banu Umayyah became their partners in the government, the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used the word ‘beginning’ for the ‘end’ of the government. Similarly, we have mentioned earlier that in this way each of them became caliph, until in 101 Hijri, Sayyiduna Umar bin Abdul Aziz passed away, so the people pledged allegiance to Yazid bin Abdul Malik. Yazid bin Abdul Malik died in the land of Sham at the place of Balqa on a Friday, which was the 25th of Sha’ban, 105 Hijri, so the people pledged allegiance to Hisham bin Abdul Malik, who was his brother, on the same day. Then Hisham appointed Khalid bin Abdullah Qasri as the governor of Iraq. He deposed Umar bin Hubayrah at the beginning of 106 Hijri, so the callers of Banu Abbas appeared in Khurasan. They pledged allegiance to Sulayman bin Kathir Khuzai, who was the one inviting towards Banu Hashim. He set out towards Makkah in 106 Hijri, so the people pledged allegiance to him for Banu Hashim. In this way, the government of Banu Umayyah became corrupt and Banu Hashim again became their partners in it, so the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used the word ‘beginning’ for the ‘end’ of their government. The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If they remain, then their religion will remain for them for seventy years. By this, he meant the situation they were in before that."
"6664","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""After me, the first of you to join me will be the one whose hand is the longest."" Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that all the wives of the Prophet measured their hands to see whose hand was the longest. Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that Lady Zainab (may Allah be pleased with her) had the longest hand, because she used to work with her hand and give (its earnings) in charity."
"6665","One who has the longest hands amongst you would meet me most immediately. She farther said: They (the wives of Allah's Apostle) used to measure the hands as to whose hand was the longest and it was the hand of Zainab that was the longest amongst them, as she used to work with her hand and Spend (that income) on charity. (Using translation from Muslim 2452)"
"6666","""Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""A time will come upon the people, when a group of people will wage a holy war and it will be said, 'Is there amongst you anyone who has accompanied Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' They will say, 'Yes.' And so victory will be bestowed on them. Then a time will come upon the people when a group of people will wage a holy war, and it will be said, ""Is there amongst you anynone who has accompanied the companions of Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' They will say, 'Yes.' And so victory will be bestowed on them. Then a time will come upon the people when a group of people will wage a holy war, and it will be said, ""Is there amongst you anyone who has been in the company of the companions of the companions of Messenger of Allah ﷺ ?' They will say, 'Yes.' And victory will be bestowed on them."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 3649)"
"6667","What made you laugh. Messenger of Allah? He said: Some people from my Umma were presented to me who were fighters in the way of Allah and were sailing in this sea. (Gliding smoothly on the water), they appeared to be kings or like kings (sitting) on thrones (the narrator has a doubt about the actual expression used by the Holy Prophet). She said: Messenger of Allah, pray to Allah that He may include me among these warriors. He prayed for her. Then he placed his head (down) and dozed off (again). He woke up laughing, as before. (She said) I said: Messenger of Allah, what makes you laugh? He replied: A people from my Umma were presented to me. They were fighters in Allah's way. (He described them in the same words as he had described the first warriors.) She said: Messenger of Allah, pray to God that He may include me among these warriors. He said: You are among the first ones. Umm Haram daughter of Milhan sailed in the aea in the time of Mu'awiya. When she came out of the sea and (was going to mount a riding animal) she fell down and died. (Using translation from Muslim 1912a)"
"6668","I became drowsy. He said: O Abu Dharr! If all people adopt this, it will be sufficient for them. Then he said: O Abu Dharr, what will you do when you are expelled from Madinah? I said: I will try, as much as I am able, to become like a pigeon of Makkah (i.e., I will move to Makkah). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: What will you do when you are expelled from Makkah as well? I said: I will try, according to my ability and status, to go towards the land of Shaam and the sacred land. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: What will you do when you are expelled from there as well? I said: In that case, by the One Who sent you with the truth, I will take my sword and hang it around my neck (and start fighting those people). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Is it not better than this that you obey and follow that Abyssinian slave with a cut nose and ears (who will be the ruler at that time)?"
"6669","The Prophet said:) One of you will die in a wilderness, but a group of believers will attend his funeral prayer. (Sayyiduna Abu Dharr Ghifari (may Allah be pleased with him) said:) Each of those people died in a populated area. Only I am about to die in a wilderness. By Allah! Neither have I lied nor has anyone lied to me. You keep watch on the road. Sayyida Umm Zar said: Now the pilgrims have departed and the roads have been cut off. Sayyiduna Abu Dharr Ghifari (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Go and check the road. Sayyida Umm Zar (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: I came to the hill, I checked, then I returned to him and began to nurse him. While I was nursing him, suddenly some people arrived there riding their mounts. It seemed as if they were birds. They came and stopped near me. They asked: O bondwoman of Allah, what is your matter? I said to them: A Muslim man is about to die, will you shroud him? They asked: Who is he? I replied: Sayyiduna Abu Dharr. They asked: The one who is the companion of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)? I replied: Yes. Sayyida Umm Zar (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Then they said: May our parents be sacrificed for him. Then they quickly went to Sayyiduna Abu Dharr Ghifari (may Allah be pleased with him) and presented themselves to him. Sayyiduna Abu Dharr Ghifari (may Allah be pleased with him) welcomed them and said: I heard the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say to some people among whom I was present: “One of you will die in a wilderness, but a group of believers will attend his funeral.” (Sayyiduna Abu Dharr Ghifari (may Allah be pleased with him) said:) Each of those people died in a town or among a gathering of people. Only I am about to die in a wilderness. Listen, if I have enough cloth for my shroud or my wife has enough cloth, then only shroud me in my or my wife’s cloth. Listen, I make you witnesses that none among you who is an amir, or an ‘arif, or a barid, or a naqib (i.e., anyone holding any position or rank) should shroud me. (The narrator says:) There was not a single person among those present who had not held some position. Only one young Ansari was there. He said: O uncle, I will give you the shroud and I will not include that which you have mentioned. I will shroud you in my own sheet and in the two garments I am wearing underneath, which my mother spun for me with her own hands. So that Ansari shrouded Sayyiduna Abu Dharr Ghifari (may Allah be pleased with him) in the presence of those people. Among those present were Sayyiduna Hajar bin Adbar and Malik bin Ashter. All these people were from Yemen."
"6670","The woman replied: Sayyiduna Abu Dharr. They said: The companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)? I replied: Yes. So they said: May my parents be sacrificed for him. Then they quickly went to Sayyiduna Abu Dharr Ghifari (may Allah be pleased with him) and presented themselves to him. Sayyiduna Abu Dharr Ghifari (may Allah be pleased with him) said to them: Glad tidings for you. I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say to some people, among whom I was also present: ""One of you will die in a deserted place, and a group of believers will attend his funeral."" Then Sayyiduna Abu Dharr Ghifari (may Allah be pleased with him) said: (Except for me) each of them died among people (now only I am left). By Allah! I have neither lied nor has anyone lied to me. If I have enough cloth for my shroud or my wife has enough cloth, then only in my or my wife's cloth should I be shrouded. I ask you by Allah, none of you should shroud me who is an amir, or an 'arif, or a barid, or a naqib (i.e., a government official). There was no one among those present who did not hold one of these positions, except for one Ansari youth. He said: O uncle! I will shroud you. I will shroud you in this sheet of mine and in these two garments which my mother prepared for me. So Sayyiduna Abu Dharr Ghifari (may Allah be pleased with him) said: You shroud me. So that Ansari, in the presence of those present, shrouded Sayyiduna Abu Dharr Ghifari (may Allah be pleased with him), took care of his (washing, etc.) affairs, and those same people buried Sayyiduna Abu Dharr Ghifari (may Allah be pleased with him). All of them were from Yemen."
"6671","I asked Sayyiduna Nafi’ bin Utbah bin Abi Waqqas. I said: Tell me, did you hear the Prophet (peace be upon him) mention the Dajjal? He replied: I was present with the Prophet (peace be upon him). At that time, some people from the West were present with him. They had come to accept Islam. They were wearing woolen clothes. When I came close to the Prophet (peace be upon him), I heard him say: ""You will fight against the people of the Arabian Peninsula, and Allah will grant you victory over them. Then you will fight against the people of Persia, and Allah will grant you victory over them. Then you will fight against the Romans, and Allah will grant you victory over them. Then you will fight against the Dajjal, and Allah will grant you victory over him."
"6672","The Shaykh says: The word «» means to come hastily."
"6673","I heard Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, ""Yemen will be conquered and some people will migrate (from Medina) and will urge their families, and those who will obey them to migrate (to Yemen) although Medina will be better for them; if they but knew. Sham will also be conquered and some people will migrate (from Medina) and will urge their families and those who will obey them, to migrate (to Sham) although Medina will be better for them; if they but knew. 'Iraq will be conquered and some people will migrate (from Medina) and will urge their families and those who will obey them to migrate (to 'Iraq) although Medina will be better for them; if they but knew."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 1875)"
"6674","The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: All of you. I entered inside and found him performing ablution slowly and calmly. Then he said: O Awf, remember six things that will happen before the Day of Judgment. One of them is my death. Awf narrates: Hearing this, I was shocked. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Say: One. I said: One. Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Bayt al-Maqdis will be conquered, then a disease will spread among you, then wealth will increase among you to the extent that if one of you is given a hundred dirhams, he will still be displeased, then a tribulation will appear among you such that no house of a believer will remain except that the tribulation will enter it, then there will be a truce between you and Banu Asfar (i.e., the Romans), but they will break the treaty with you, then they will gather against you under eighty flags, under each flag will be twelve thousand men."
"6675","“I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the campaign of Tabuk, when he was in a tent made of leather, so I sat in front of the tent. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘Enter, O ‘Awf.’ I said, ‘All of me, O Messenger of Allah?’ He said: ‘All of you.’ Then he said: ‘O ‘Awf, remember six things (that will occur) before the Hour comes, one of which is my death.’ I was very shocked and saddened at that. He said: ‘Count that as the first. Then (will come) the conquest of Baitul-Maqdis (Jerusalem); then a disease which will appear among you and cause you and your offspring to die as martyrs and will purify your deeds; then there will be (much) wealth among you, so that if a man were to be given one hundred Dinar he would still be dissatisfied; and there will be tribulation among you that will not leave any Muslim house untouched;* then there will be a treaty between you and the Romans, then they will betray you and march against you with eighty banners, under each of which will be twelve thousand (troops).’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4042)"
"6676","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""Soon you will go to a people whose hair will be curly, so accept admonition regarding them, for they will be a strength for you and, by Allah’s permission, will bring you to your enemy."" (The narrator says:) By this, the Copts of Egypt are meant."
"6677","I have no need for this charity."
"6678","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said to me: O ‘Adi bin Hatim, accept Islam, you will be safe. I said: I have my own religion. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: I know more about your religion than you. He said this two or three times, then he said: Are you not the chief of your people? I replied: Yes. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) asked: Do you not take a quarter of the war booty? I replied: Yes. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Then this is not permissible for you in your religion. Sayyiduna ‘Adi (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I felt ashamed at this, so the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: O ‘Adi bin Hatim, accept Islam, you will be safe. Then the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: I think (the narrator is unsure, perhaps these are the words), I believe, or as the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: You are not accepting Islam because you see around me people who are needy. Soon, a woman will ride from Hira without anyone’s protection until she performs tawaf of the Ka‘bah, and the treasures of Kisra bin Hurmuz will be opened for us, and wealth will become abundant, until a person will wish that someone would accept his wealth as charity from him. Sayyiduna ‘Adi bin Hatim (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I saw a woman who rode from Hira without anyone’s protection until she performed tawaf of the Ka‘bah, and I was among the first army that attacked the treasures of Kisra bin Hurmuz in Mada’in, and I swear by the name of Allah that the third thing will also certainly come true which the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) told me."
"6679","I have no interest in it."
"6680","The Hour will not be established until wealth becomes abundant and increases, to the extent that a person will take out the zakat of his wealth but will not find anyone who will accept it from him."
"6681","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In the last part of my Ummah, there will be a caliph who will give handfuls of wealth without counting."
"6682","""We were in the company of Jabir b. 'Abdullah that he said it may happen that the people of Iraq may not send their qafiz and dirhams (their measures of food stuff and their money). We said: Who would be responsible for it? He said: The non-Arabs would prevent them. He again said: There is the possibility that the people of Syria may not send their dinars and mudds. We said: Who would be responsible for it? He said this prevention would be made by the Romans. He (Jabir b. Abdullah) kept quiet for a while and then reported Messenger of Allah ﷺ having said there would be a caliph in the last (period) of my Ummah who would freely give handfuls of wealth to the people without counting it. I said to Abu Nadra and Abu al-'Ala: Do you mean 'Umar b. 'Abd al-Aziz? They said: No (he would be Imam Mahdi). (Using translation from Muslim 2913a)"
"6683","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: Have you made cushions ? I said: How can we afford cushions ? He said: Soon you will have cushions. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4145)"
"6684","I am still not left alone? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then go to those with whom you have a connection (i.e., go to your tribe) and stay among them. Sayyiduna Abu Dharr al-Ghifari (may Allah be pleased with him) asked: Should I take up my weapon? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: In that case, you will become a partner with those people in this matter. If you fear that the flash of the sword will frighten you, then place the edge of your cloak over your face, so that person will bear the burden of his and your sin (who kills you)."
"6685","I want to unite them on one word, because of which the Arabs will be subservient to them and the non-Arabs will pay them jizya."" They asked: ""What is that word?"" The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""La ilaha illallah (There is no god but Allah)."" So those people stood up and said: ""Do you want to make all the gods into one god?"" The narrator says: So regarding this, this verse was revealed: "" Saad. By the Qur'an, full of reminder."" up to "" Indeed, this is a very astonishing thing."
"6686","narrates: He heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) saying: ""A group of Muslims will surely conquer the treasures of the family of Kisra."
"6687","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You will come face to face with one another, you will envy one another, you will turn your backs on one another, you will bear malice against one another, then soon you will go towards the poor emigrants and some of them you will make ride on the necks of others."
"6688","“When the treasures of Persia and Rome are opened for you, what kind of people will you be?” ‘Abdur-Rahman bin ‘Awf said: “We will say what Allah has commanded us to say.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Or something other than that. You will compete with one another, then you will envy one another, then you will turn your backs on one another, then you will hate one another, or something like that. Then you will go to the poor among the Muhajirun and appoint some of them as leaders of others.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3996)"
"6689","Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""When Khosrau is ruined, there will be no Khosrau after him; and when Caesar is ruined, there will be no Caesar after him. By Him in Whose Hands my life is, you will spend their treasures in Allah's Cause."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 3120)"
"6690","""When Kisra is ruined, there will be no Kisra after him, and when Caesar is ruined, there will be no Caesar after him. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! You shall spend their treasures in Allah's cause."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2216)"
"6691","The Hour will not be established until a mountain of gold emerges from the Euphrates River, over which people will fight one another, and out of every ten men, nine will be killed."
"6692","“The Hour will not begin until the Euphrates uncovers a mountain of gold and people fight over it, and out of every ten, nine will be killed.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4046)"
"6693","The Euphrates is soon to uncover a treasure of gold, but those who are present must not take any of it. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4313)"
"6696","“The Hour will not begin until the Euphrates uncovers a mountain of gold and people fight over it, and out of every ten, nine will be killed.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4046)"
"6697",""" The earth will throw out pieces of its liver(in sides): liver; gold and silver will come out like columns."" He said: ""A thief will come and say: 'For this my hands were amputated?' A murderer will come and say: 'For this I killed?' One who severed ties of kinship will come and say: 'For this I severed the ties of kinship?' Then they will leave it without taking anything from it.""' (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2208)"
"6698","We complained to Messenger of Allah ﷺ (about our state) while he was leaning against his sheet cloak in the shade of the Kaʿba. We said, ""Will you ask Allah to help us? Will you invoke Allah for us?"" He said, ""Among those who were before you a (believer) used to be seized and, a pit used to be dug for him and then he used to be placed in it. Then a saw used to be brought and put on his head which would be split into two halves. His flesh might be combed with iron combs and removed from his bones, yet, all that did not cause him to revert from his religion. By Allah! This religion (Islam) will be completed (and triumph) till a rider (traveler) goes from Sanʿa' (the capital of Yemen) to Hadramout fearing nobody except Allah and the wolf lest it should trouble his sheep, but you are impatient."" (See Hadith No. 191, Vol. 5) (Using translation from Bukhārī 6943)"
"6699","The Hour will not be established until killing becomes widespread and until the land of the Arabs returns to being meadows and rivers."
"6700","I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""There will not remain any house, whether made of mud or of bricks, on the face of the earth in which Allah will not have made the word of Islam enter, whether that (house) belongs to a powerful person or to a lesser person."
"6701","The Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Allahu Akbar! This is just like what the Children of Israel said to Sayyiduna Musa, peace be upon him: “Appoint for us a god just as they have gods.” Sayyiduna Musa, peace be upon him, said: “You are a people who are ignorant.” Then the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: You will surely follow the ways of those before you."
"6702","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Who else?"
"6703","The Prophet ﷺ said, ""You will follow the wrong ways, of your predecessors so completely and literally that if they should go into the hole of a mastigure, you too will go there."" We said, ""O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! Do you mean the Jews and the Christians?"" He replied, ""Whom else?"" (Meaning, of course, the Jews and the Christians.) (Using translation from Bukhārī 3456)"
"6704","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) mentioned and said: ""Destruction is for the Arabs because of an evil that has drawn near; it will come in the form of a blind, mute, and deaf tribulation. In it, the one who is sitting will be better than the one who is standing, the one who is standing will be better than the one who is walking, and the one who is walking will be better than the one who is running. And for the one who runs in it, there will be destruction from Allah Almighty on the Day of Resurrection."",""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ  said"",""""""Hasten to perform good deeds before a time comes upon you like the dark night. During that time"","" a person will be a believer in the morning and a disbeliever in the evening"","" or he will be a believer in the evening and a disbeliever in the morning. He will sell his religion for worldly gains."""""""
"6705","The trustworthy person will be accused, and the one who is not trustworthy will be made trustworthy, and the ignoble will be made to sit among you."" They asked: ""O Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him! What is meant by the ignoble?"" The Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Such tribulations as will be like pieces of a dark night."
"6706","I were in the place of this (dead person).'"
"6707","The Last Hour would not come until a person would pass by a grave of another person and he would say: I wish it had been my abode. (Using translation from Muslim 157k)"
"6708","The cross has prevailed.' A man from among the Muslims will say: 'Rather, Allah Almighty has granted victory.' Then they will fight each other. The cross will not be far from the Muslims. A man from among the Muslims will advance towards it and break it. Then the Romans will advance towards the one who broke the cross and will behead him. Then the Muslims will go towards their weapons and the fighting will begin. Allah Almighty will honor them with martyrdom. The Romans will go to their king and say: 'We are sufficient for you to attack the Arabian Peninsula.' Then they will gather for war and come under banners, under each banner there will be twelve thousand men."
"6709","The people asked: ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! What is meant by 'Harj'?"" The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Killing and bloodshed."" The people said: ""Will it be more than what we have killed?"" The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not your killing of the polytheists, rather it will be killing one another."" The people asked: ""(At that time) will our intellects remain with us?"" The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The intellects of the people of that time will be taken away."
"6710","The people asked: ""O Messenger of Allah! What is meant by harj?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: ""Killing, killing."
"6711","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: The time will become short, knowledge will be decreased, civil strife (fitan) will appear, niggardliness will be case into people's heart, and harj will be prevalent. He was asked: Messenger of Allah! what is it: He replied: Slaughter, slaughter. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4255)"
"6712","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) saying to Marwan bin Hakam: My beloved, the truthful and trustworthy, Sayyiduna Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings be upon him) has told me this: ""Corruption in my Ummah will be through the foolish youths of the Quraysh."
"6713","The Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said:) Some tribes of my Ummah will return to the Turks and to the worshippers of idols. And what I fear most for my Ummah is the misguiding rulers. When the sword is placed among them, it will not be lifted from them until the Day of Resurrection. And soon, about thirty great liars will appear in my Ummah. I am the Seal of the Prophets; there is no prophet after me. A group from my Ummah will always remain steadfast upon the truth and will continue to be helped, until the command of Allah the Exalted comes."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The correct word in the narration is ""shirk"" (polytheism)."
"6714","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: Allah, the Exalted, folded for me the earth, or he said (the narrator is doubtful): My Lord folded for me the earth, so much so that I saw its easts and wests (i.e. the extremities). The kingdom of my community will reach as far as the earth was floded for me. The two treasures, the red and the white, were bestowed on me. I prayed to my Lord that He may not destroy my community by prevailing famine, and not give their control to an enemy who annihilates then en masse except from among themselves. My Lord said to me: Muhammad, If I make a decision, it is not withdrawn ; and I shall not destroy them by prevailing famine, and I shall not give their control to an enemy, except from among themselves, who exterminates them en masse, even if they are stormed from all sides of the earth ; only a section of them will destroy another section, and a section will captive another section. I am afraid about my community of those leaders who will lead astray. When the sword is used among my people, it will not be withdrawn from them till the Day of Resurrection, and the Last Hour will not come before the tribes of my people attach themselves to the polytheists and tribes of my people worship idols. There will be among my people thirty great liars each of them asserting that he is (Allah's) prophet, where as I am the seal of the Prophet s after whom (me) there will be no prophet ; and a section of my people will continue to hold to the truth - (according to the Ibn Isa's version: (will continue to dominate) - the agreed version goes: ""and will not be injured by those who oppose them, till Allah's command comes."" (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4252)"
"6715","narrates this statement of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When my Ummah will walk with pride and the people of Persia and Rome become their servants, then one among them will be given authority over the others (that is, the Ummah will fall into mutual discord)."
"6716","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Time will contract, knowledge will decrease, tribulations will appear, and killing (harj) will increase greatly.\"" The people asked: \""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! What is meant by harj?\"" The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: \""Killing.\"""""
"6717","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: The time will become short, knowledge will be decreased, civil strife (fitan) will appear, niggardliness will be case into people's heart, and harj will be prevalent. He was asked: Messenger of Allah! what is it: He replied: Slaughter, slaughter. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4255)"
"6718","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah will not take away knowledge by snatching it from the people, but He will take away knowledge by taking away the scholars along with their knowledge, until when no scholar remains, people will take the ignorant as leaders. They will be asked questions and they will give answers without knowledge. They will go astray and will lead others astray as well."
"6719","the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Allah will not take away knowledge by removing it from people (from their hearts). Rather He will take away knowledge by taking away the scholars, then when there are no scholars left, the people will take the ignorant as their leaders. They will be asked questions and they will issue verdicts without knowledge, thus they will go astray and lead others astray.'"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 52)"
"6720","The world will not come to an end until the children of the lowly are with the lowly."
"6721","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""People will continue to ask questions until someone will say: Allah created the creation, so who created Allah?"
"6722","narrates this statement of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Indeed, Allah will not take away knowledge by snatching it from the people, while He has granted them knowledge. Rather, He will take away knowledge by taking the souls of the scholars, until when no scholar remains, people will take the ignorant as leaders. They will ask them questions, and they will give answers without knowledge. They will misguide others and will themselves be misguided."
"6723","narrator is doubtful about a word), as long as they do not argue about children and destiny."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) Here, by children, it is meant the children of the polytheists (i.e., the debate about what will be their fate in the Hereafter)."
"6724","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us while we were reciting (the Qur’an). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All praise and thanks are due to Allah alone. The Book of Allah is one. Among you are red, white, and black people. You should continue to recite it before there come people who will recite it and assign to it a price as is assigned to a portion."
"6725","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ one day came out to us while we were reciting the Qur’an. He said: Praise be to Allah. The Book of Allah is one, and among you are the red, and among you are the white and among you are the black. Recite it before there appear people who will recite it and straighten it as an arrow is straightened. They will get their reward for it in this world and will not get it in the Hereafter. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 831)"
"6726","The best people are those of my generation, then those who come after them, then those who come after them. Then there will come people whose oaths will precede their testimony and whose testimony will precede their oaths."
"6727","I am standing among you today, the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) stood among us. He (peace be upon him) said: Treat my companions well, then those who come after them, then those who come after them, then those who come after them. Then lying will become widespread, to the extent that a man will give testimony on an oath about which he was not even asked. So whoever wants to enter Paradise should adhere to the (Muslim) community, for indeed Satan is with one person and is farther from two. And no man should ever be alone with a woman, for the third among them will be Satan. And whoever finds goodness pleasing and evil displeasing is a believer."
"6728","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood before us as I am standing before you, and said: ʿI urge you to show respect to my Companions, then those who come after them, then those who come after them, then lying will become so widespread that a man will start to give testimony before he is asked to do so.Whoever among you wants to attain a spacious abode in Paradise, let him adhere to the jama'ah (main body of Muslims), for the Shaitan is with the one who is alone, but he is further away from two. And no one of you should be alone with a woman for the Shaitan will be the third one present. The one who is pleased with his good deeds and upset by his bad deeds is a believer.ʿ (Using translation from Aḥmad 114)"
"6729","the best of my people is the generation in which I have been sent, then their immediate followers, then their immediate followers. Allah knows best whether he mentioned the third or not. After them will be people who will give testimony without being asked, who will make vows which they do not fulfill, who will be treacherous and not to be trusted, among whom fatness will appear. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4657)"
"6730","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Indeed, the Jews were divided into 71 sects (the narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words) or were divided into 72 sects, and the Christians were likewise, and this nation will be divided into 73 sects."
"6731","I think I should return. People said: Stay, may Allah have mercy on you, move forward so that the Muslims may see you, perhaps Allah will bring about some good because of you. Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: I think I should return, because I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""What will be the state of one of you (i.e., the wives of the Prophet) when the dogs of Haw'ab will bark at her."
"6732","The same thing was also said to me by the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). Abu Aswad says: I thought to myself, I have never seen anyone like him on a day like today—someone who is a warrior and yet speaks to people in the manner that he does (he meant Sayyiduna Ali, may Allah be pleased with him)."
"6733","The Hour will not be established until two great groups fight each other, and there will be a great battle between them, and the claim of both will be the same."
"6734","The last Hour will not come until the two parties (of Muslims) confront each other and there is a large-scale massacre amongst them and the claim of both of them is the same. (Using translation from Muslim 157i)"
"6735","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""A rebellious group will kill Ammar."
"6736","A band of rebels would kill ʿAmmar. (Using translation from Muslim 2916c)"
"6737","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, after me in my Ummah (here the narrator is doubtful about a word) there will be some people who will recite the Qur'an, but it will not go beyond their throats. They will go out of the religion just as an arrow passes through its target, and then they will not return to the religion. They will be the worst of all creation and the universe."
"6738","narrate to you any hadith from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then for me, falling down from the sky is more beloved than attributing any false statement to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And when I speak to you about anything between myself and you, then war is the name of deception. I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""In the last era, some people will come whose ages will be young and whose intellects will be immature. They will narrate the sayings of the best person among the creation, but they will exit from the religion just as an arrow passes through its target. Their faith will not go beyond their throats. Wherever you encounter them, kill them, for the one who kills them will have a reward on the Day of Resurrection."
"6739","When I mention a tradition to you from the Messenger of Allah (May peace be upon him), it is dearer to me that I fall from the heaven than I lie on him. But when I talk to you about matters between me and you, then war is a deception. I heard the Messenger of Allah (May peace be upon him) say: Towards the end of the time there will be people who are young in age and from Islam as an arrow goes through the animal aimed at, and their faith will not pass their throats. Wherever you meet them kill them, for their killing will bring a reward for him who kills them on the day of Resurrection. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4767)"
"6740","I do not act justly, then who will act justly? Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) stood up and said: O Messenger of Allah! Allow me regarding him so that I may strike his neck. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave him, for he will have companions such that you will consider your prayers insignificant compared to their prayers, and your fasts insignificant compared to their fasts. They will recite the Qur'an, but it will not go beyond their throats. They will go out of Islam just as an arrow passes through its target. When its tip is examined, nothing is found there; when its edge is examined, nothing is found there; when its binding (the place where the string is tied to the arrowhead) is examined, nothing is found there; when its nadi (the part between the arrowhead and the feathers) is examined, nothing is found there, though it has surpassed dung and blood. (The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said:) The specific sign of these people is a black-skinned man whose one arm will be like a woman's breast, and it will be like a shaking piece of flesh. These people will appear at the time of discord among the people. Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I bear witness to this: We heard this from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I also bear witness to this: Sayyiduna Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) fought against these people, and I was with Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) at that time. Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) ordered that this man be searched for, and he was found. When he was brought and I examined him, he was exactly as the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had described him."
"6741","When we were in the company of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he was distributing the spoils of war, there came to him Dhul-Khuwasira, one of Banu Tamim. He said: Messenger of Allah, do justice. Upon this the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Woe be upon thee! Who would do justice, if I do not do justice? You would be unsuccessful and incurring a loss, if I do not do justice. Upon this Umar b. Khattab (Allah be pleased with him) said: Messenger of Allah, permit me to strike off his neck. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Leave him, for he has friends (who would outwardly look to be so religious and pious) that everyone among you would consider his prayer insignificant as compared with their prayer, and his fast as compared with their fasts. They would recite the Qur'an but it would not go beyond their collar-bones. They would pass through (the teachings of Islam so hurriedly) just as the arrow passes through the prey. He would look at its Iron head, but would not find anything ticking) there. He would then see at the lowest end, but would not find anything sticking there. He would then see at its grip but would not find anything sticking to it. He would then see at its feathers and he would find nothing sticking to them (as the arrow would pass so quickly that nothing would stick to it) neither excrement nor blood. They would be recognised by the presence of a black man among them whose upper arms would be like a woman's breast, or like a piece of meat as it quivers, and they would come forth at the time when there is dissension among the people. Abu Sai'd said: I testify to the fact that I heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I testify to the fact that 'Ali b. Abu Talib fought against them and I was with him. He gave orders about that man who was sought for, and when he was brought in, and when I looked at him, he was exactly as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had described him. (Using translation from Muslim 1064f)"
"6742","The angel of Rain sought permission from Allah to visit the Prophet ﷺ and that was the day of Umm Salamah. The Prophet ﷺ said to Umm Salamah, ""Guard the door for us so that no one should enter."" Then when she was at the door, al-Ḥusayn b. ʿAlī came and pushed the door open forcefully. He entered and began to leap on the back of the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet lovingly hugged and kissed him. The angel asked him, ""Do you love him?"" He replied, ""Yes."" The angel said, 'However, your Ummah will kill him. If you wish, I can show you the place where he will be killed."" He said, ""Yes."" So, the angel took a handful of ˹the soil from˺ the place where he will be killed and showed it to him; he brought him sandy or red soil. Umm Salamah took that soil and kept it in her garment."
"6743","The Hour will not be established until you fight against a people whose eyes will be small and whose faces will be like shields made of leather."
"6744","The Hour will not be established until the Muslims fight with the Turks, who are a people whose faces are like shields made of leather. They wear clothes made of hair and shoes made of hair."
"6745","The Last Hour would not come until the Muslims fight with the Turks-a people whose faces would be like hammered shields wearing clothes of hair and walking (with shoes) of hair. (Using translation from Muslim 2912d)"
"6746","The Last Hour would not come until a people wearing shoes of hair fight against you having their faces like hammered shields. (Using translation from Muslim 2912b)"
"6747","“The Hour will not begin until you fight people with small eyes and wide faces, as if their eyes are the pupils of locusts and as if their faces are hammered shields. They will be wearing shoes of hair, using leather shields and tying their horses to date-palm trees.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4099)"
"6748","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Some of my people will alight on low-lying ground, which they will call al-Basrah, beside a river called the Tigris over which there is a bridge. Its people will be numerous and it will be one of the capital cities of immigrants (or one of the capital cities of Muslims, according to the version of Ibn Yahya who reported from Abu Ma'mar). At the end of time the descendants of Qantura' will come with broad faces and small eyes and alight on the bank of the river. The town's inhabitants will then separate into three sections, one of which will follow cattle and (live in) the desert and perish, another of which will seek security for themselves and perish, but a third will put their children behind their backs and fight the invaders, and they will be the martyrs. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4306)"
"6749","The Last Hour would not come until the women of the tribe of Daus would be seen going round Dhi al-Khalasa (for worship) and Dhi al-Khalasa is a place in Tabala, where there was a temple in which the people of the tribe of Daus used to worship the idol. (Using translation from Muslim 2906)"
"6750","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man from Habasha (Abyssinia), wearing two garments, will demolish the Ka'bah."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) ""Suweiqatain"" refers to two garments."
"6751","(The above mentioned) hadith has been narrated on the authority of Abu Huraira through another chain of transmitters. (Using translation from Muslim 2909b)"
"6752","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Take benefit from this house, for it will be demolished twice and the third time it will be lifted."
"6753","narrate: They heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""There will certainly be people in my Ummah who will declare silk, alcohol, and musical instruments to be lawful."
"6754","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: An army will come to attack the Kaaba. When they reach an open field, the people at the front and the back (of the army) will be swallowed up by the earth. Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) asked: O Messenger of Allah! Among them there will be some people who are not part of them and have nothing to do with them. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: All of them will be swallowed up, then they will be resurrected (on the Day of Judgment) according to their intentions."
"6755","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: He will also be swallowed along with them, but on the Day of Resurrection, he will be raised according to the intention he had in his heart.” The narrator named Abdul Aziz says: I asked Abu Ja’far (perhaps meaning Imam Muhammad al-Baqir): Lady Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: in the open part of the earth. So Imam Abu Ja’far replied: By Allah! What is meant by this is the stony plain of Madinah."
"6756","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: At the time of the death of a caliph, there will be discord. Then a man from the people of Madinah, who is related to the Quraysh, will go towards Makkah. Some people from the people of Makkah will come to him and force him to come out, even though he will dislike it. Then they will take his pledge of allegiance between the Rukn and Maqam. Then an army from the people of Syria will be sent towards him. When they reach the place of Bayda, they will be swallowed up by the earth. When this news reaches the people, the Abdal from Syria and a group from the people of Iraq will come to him and pledge allegiance to him. Then a man from the Quraysh will come out, whose maternal relatives are from Banu Kalb. He will send an army towards them, but they will defeat that army and prevail over them. He will distribute their wealth among the people and act among them according to the Sunnah of their Prophet. That person will remain on earth for seven years. He will establish Islam firmly in the world."
"6757","The name of Sayyiduna Abu Malik Ash’ari (may Allah be pleased with him) is Harith bin Malik, and according to one opinion, the name of Sayyiduna Abu Malik Ash’ari (may Allah be pleased with him) is Ka’b bin Asim."
"6758","“People among my nation will drink wine, calling it by another name, and musical instruments will be played for them and singing girls (will sing for them). Allah will cause the earth to swallow them up, and will turn them into monkeys and pigs.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4020)"
"6759","The Hour will not be established until people boast to one another regarding (the construction of) mosques."
"6760","""The Messenger of Allah said: 'The Hour will not begin until the people compete in (building) mosques.'"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 739)"
"6761","I have seen one of them and I am waiting for the other. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) informed us that trustworthiness was sent down into the hearts of people, and the Qur'an was revealed, so they learned knowledge from the Qur'an and learned knowledge from the Sunnah. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) told us about its removal. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: A man will sleep, and trustworthiness will be taken away from his heart, until only a faint trace remains, like a mark left by a spot. Then he will sleep again, and trustworthiness will be taken away from his heart, until only a trace remains like a blister that appears on your foot due to a burning coal—you see it swollen, but there is nothing inside it. People will engage in buying and selling with one another, but hardly anyone will fulfill trust, to the extent that it will be said: There is an honest man among the tribe of so-and-so. To the extent that it will be said about a man: How strong, how clever, how wise he is, even though there will not be in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of goodness. (Sayyiduna Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, said:) A time came upon me when I did not care with whom I did business, for if he was a believer, his religion would prevent him from cheating me, and if he was a Jew or a Christian, the official would prevent him (from doing so). But now, I only do business with so-and-so and so-and-so."
"6762","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ narrated to us two ahadith. I have seen one (crystallized into reality), and I am waiting for the other. He told us: Trustworthiness descended in the innermost (root) of the hearts of people. Then the Qur'an was revealed and they learnt from the Qur'an and they learnt from the Sunnah. Then he (the Holy Prophet) told us about the removal of trustworthiness. He said: The man would have a wink of sleep and trustworthiness would be taken away from his heart leaving the impression of a faint mark. He would again sleep and trustworthiness would be taken away from his heart leaving an impression of a blister, as if you rolled down an ember on your foot and it was vesicled. He would see a swelling having nothing in it. He (the Holy Prophet) then took up a pebble and rolled it down over his foot and (said): The people would enter into transactions amongst one another and hardly a person would be left who would return (things) entrusted to him. (And there would be so much paucity of honest persons) till it would be said: There in such a such tribe is a trustworthy man. And they would also say about a person: How prudent he is, how broad-minded he is and how intelligent he is, whereas in his heart there would not be faith even to the weight of a mustard seed. I have passed through a time in which I did not care with whom amongst you I entered into a transaction, for if he were a Muslim his faith would compel him to discharge his obligations to me and it he were a Christian or a Jew, the ruler would compel him to discharge his obligations to me. But today I would not enter into a transaction with you except so and so. (Using translation from Muslim 143a)"
